  "summary": "Distinctive body modification practice where lip plates are worn by Mursi women as a symbol of beauty and social status.",
  "description": "Characterized by large clay or wooden discs inserted into a lower lip that has been pierced and stretched, creating an elongated lower lip. The aesthetic developed as a beauty ideal and social marker within Mursi society, with larger plates indicating higher social status and marriageability.",
